+Construction. Write J=[[0,I],[I,0]], the matrix of a split integral form in
+2n variables. Before any public form exists, sample a unimodular integer R and
+a rank-n/2 diagonal projector E. Put P=R^{-1}ER and C=I+(u^2-1)P^T, where u is
+a sampled power of 2. The public second form has matrix [[0,C],[C^T,0]]. Its
+relative operator is diag(C^T,C). Since P^2=P, the polynomial
+p(t)=u/(u+1)+t/(u+1) evaluates to
+diag((I+(u-1)P),(I+(u-1)P^T)), an integer matrix whose determinant is a power
+of 2 and which carries J to the second form. This is inverse generation by a
+composed projector identity; make_instance never solves an equivalence.
+
+Track B discriminator. The paper's general route is bounded matrix search.
+For this distribution an exact reference solver instead materializes the
+relative operator, extracts its two eigenvalues, interpolates the linear
